Hmm, actually one concern: deleting `<sessionCwd>/.fah/spills/<sid>/` — a session whose cwd is `/` → `.fah/spills/<sid>` at root. That's how spills are written anyway (same convention), so cleanup matches. But a WRONG cwd in a header pointing at a real project could... no — it deletes only `.fah/spills/<sid>/` — scoped to the sid dir. Safe.

I'll make spills cleanup opt-out-able for tests (`cleanWorkspaceSpills: true` default; the unit test IT-1 covers it with a fake fs).

Methods:
